[38;5;231m⏺[39m Next is the filter layout. I'm sketching it in a browser tab because the layout is easier to judge by seeing it. Your
  browser should open on its own; if it doesn't, go to:

  [94m]8;id=7faah;http://localhost:52703/?key=c8ccfe19bede8b5cc7af7ef8573ffa94bc28b070a083fe79d40cab2e8cab039e\http://localhost:52703/?key=c8ccfe19bede8b5cc7af7ef8573ffa94bc28b070a083fe79d40cab2e8cab039e[39m]8;;\

  The browser companion uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal. Its mockup files are
  saved in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m at the repo root. The repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, so I'll keep that directory out of every commit.

  The tab shows two rough layouts with the same three controls in each:

  - [1mA, everything visible.[0m Search and Week sit side by side, with the nine event types as a wrapped checkbox list
    underneath. Failed sign-ins is one click away. Below the filters are a "Showing N of M events" count and a Clear
    filters button.
  - [1mB, compact bar plus popover.[0m Search, Week and an "Event types" button share one row. Event types open in a popover,
    and each selected type shows as a removable tag. The table starts higher on the page, but failed sign-ins takes two
    clicks.

  I recommend A. Your two most common lookups are type filters, so the type list should be visible without opening
  anything. The popover in B also adds a component to build and test for keyboard use and screen readers.

  Have a look, click the one you prefer if you like, and tell me here what you think.

